speechtext:
The amounts of money in this item are: For the maritimes, $5,000; Quebec, about $15,000; Royal Winter Fair, $35,000; Vancouver, $10,000. That makes up the $65,000. Those are amounts for buildings. We entered into a contract with the exhibition board of Vancouver to spend a certain amount of money on buildings over a period of years. The amount to be paid is $10,000 a year;
Supply-A griculture

$100,000 is to be paid over ten years, so that $10,000 is to be paid this year. There is not any way that we can get out of that obligation unless we say that we intend to go back on the contract we made. No grants are being paid to any association in British Columbia or anywhere else in Canada at present for the conducting of fairs; we are simply carrying out our obligations under a building contract "which was entered into some years ago.
